---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { collective } from '../commissions';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---
<Base title="Studio" current="studio" description="About Maison Null, a design house in Singapore with a collective of specialists behind it.">
  <section class="banner">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h1>Studio</h1>
      <p class="lede">Maison Null is a design house in Singapore. It designs brands and builds the digital products behind them, for a small number of clients at a time, and calls on a collective of specialists when a project needs more.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap cols">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>The name</h2>
        <p>A maison is a house where things are made by hand. Null is the value a program holds before anything has been put there. Every project here starts as that empty screen, and the job of the house is to fill it with something worth keeping.</p>
        <h2>Who we picture</h2>
        <p>For three years in school, the studio's lead went out every quarter with a volunteer group to visit elderly residents, in their own neighbourhoods and at homes for the aged. When we decide what goes on a screen, they are who we picture: people who were never the target user. If something works for them, it usually works for everyone else too.</p>
        <h2>One lead, and a collective</h2>
        <p>{collective.lede}</p>
        <dl class="roles">
          {collective.roles.map((r) => (<div><dt>{r.name}</dt><dd>{r.text}</dd></div>))}
        </dl>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2 class="h-rules">How the house works</h2>
        <ul class="rules">
          <li>Design first. Decide how it should look and feel before writing the code.</li>
          <li>Put AI where judgement is needed, and keep it out where correctness is needed.</li>
          <li>Build things that degrade instead of breaking: a second provider, a fallback, offline data underneath.</li>
          <li>Say plainly what is real and what is not. No invented numbers, no hidden fakery.</li>
          <li>You own what you commission: the domain, the accounts and the code.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="btns"><a class="btn solid" href={`${base}/contact/`}>Start a project</a></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
<style>
  .cols{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.2fr) minmax(0,1fr);gap:clamp(2.5rem,6vw,5rem)}
  .h-rules{font-size:clamp(1.7rem,3vw,2.2rem);margin-bottom:1.2rem}
  .rules{list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0}
  .rules li{padding:1rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);font-size:1.05rem}
  .rules li:first-child{border-top:1px solid var(--ink)}
  .cols h2{font-size:clamp(1.9rem,3.2vw,2.6rem)}
  .roles{margin:1.2rem 0 0}
  .roles div{border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding:.8rem 0}
  .roles dt{font-weight:600}
  .roles dd{margin:.15rem 0 0;color:var(--ink-soft)}
  @media (max-width:860px){.cols{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
</style>
